# Freelance Proposal Agent — Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
This is a multi-agent AI system that generates tailored freelance proposals using the Anthropic Claude API. It analyzes job postings and produces compelling, personalized proposals.

## Architecture
- `agents/` — Specialized agent modules (analyzer, writer, reviewer)
- `tools/` — Tool definitions for Claude's tool use API
- `templates/` — Proposal templates and prompt templates
- `utils/` — Shared utilities (file I/O, formatting, logging)
- `outputs/` — Generated proposals (git-ignored)

## Code Style
- Python 3.10+
- Use type hints on all functions and class methods
- Prefer dataclasses or Pydantic models over raw dicts for structured data
- Keep functions small and single-purpose
- No comments explaining what code does — only why when non-obvious

## Claude API Usage
- Always use the latest Claude model (claude-sonnet-4-6 or claude-opus-4-7)
- Enable prompt caching on system prompts and large static content
- Use structured tool use for extracting structured data from job posts
- Handle API errors gracefully with informative messages
- Never hardcode API keys — always read from environment variables

## Agent Design
- Each agent has a single responsibility
- Agents communicate via well-typed Python objects, not raw strings
- The orchestrator in `main.py` coordinates agent execution
- Use streaming where response latency matters

## Environment
- Store secrets in `.env` (never commit)
- Use `python-dotenv` to load environment variables
- Required env var: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`

## Testing
- Write tests for utility functions and tool definitions
- Mock Anthropic API calls in tests
- Place tests in a `tests/` directory mirroring the source structure
